rence to the air pollution  around our school yeah like us  there'll be a chilly start for some on  wednesday with a grass frost possible in  parts of eastern england  early low cloud and fog will slowly lift  to leave sunny spells for many thicker  clouds over parts of southern and  western britain will be stubborn to  clear giving some patchy light rain in  places  that rain will become increasingly  confined to the northwest during the  afternoon  we've got clean atlantic air moving in  on the westerly flow so the air  pollution index where one means low  pollution and 10 means very high will  stay low everywhere  the air quality report sponsored by  philips air purifiers  hello and welcome back to the daily  climate show on sky news and we're  getting straight to discussing the  climate issues of the day now with dr  cece hu program fellow of the labor and  work life programme at harvard law  school and senior associate at the  energy and climate intelligence unit and  environmental consultant richard black  so good to see you both welcome welcome  so ahead of cop 26 which we've heard  about on this and most other editions of  our show there's another big un  conference taking place cop 15 on  biodiversity is hosted by china and is  taking place virtually now world leaders  are discussing how to protect and slow  the loss of nature  it's widely believed that climate change  is a primary driver for biodiversity  loss so how important is it that we  tackle the two issues together cece i'll  put that to you  first of all what is the link between  biodiversity and climate change and does  it make sense to you that they're dealt  with together  um thank you for having me um so  biodiversity is closely linked to  climate change in two ways number one  that climate change um reduces  biodiversity and this is because um  temperature rises are now means that  plants and animals are struggling to  survive and the second way in which like  climate change is linked to biodi